  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nSunday-Next Week:\nThe ridge across the Four Corners will slowly build east into\nearly next week, with a gradual warm up in the forecast. This\ngradual warm up will feature highs returning to the lower to\nmiddle 80s by Wednesday. Confidence is high in the return of\nabove normal temperatures, with small interquartile spreads\ndepicted in the NBM. Furthermore, increasing mid-level heights\nbeyond Wednesday will support highs into the middle to upper 80s\nby late week. This pattern will support temperatures 10+ \ndegrees above normal in addition to dry weather. No mentionable \nPoPs exist through the end of next week, which will further \namplify drought conditions across portions of the Ozarks. This \nis especially true for locations that missed out on recent \nbeneficial rainfall. CPC hints at the dry and warm weather \npersisting through early to mid October.",
